{"_doc": "Bird species of Lyudmilovsk: the one table every bird system reads (C++ UBirdSpeciesLibrary, blender/birds/build_bird.py, bird life, befriending, bird flight). Sizes are adult averages from field guides. Names are localization keys bird.<key>.name. FlightStyle: Flapping (steady beats), Bounding (bursts of beats, then folded wings: tits, finches, sparrows), Undulating (beats with short glides: thrushes, woodpecker-like dips), Clapping (pigeons: fast beats, wing clap on takeoff, glides with wings raised), Soaring (gulls: slow beats, long glides, uses wind), Flicker (swifts, swallows, martins: rapid flickering beats between long sickle-wing glides). Gait: Hop, Walk, Both, Cling (swift: never lands on the ground). Clip Flap is one wingbeat over exactly 1 s: play it at rate WingbeatHz. Hop and Walk are one stride over 1 s too: play at rate speed / StrideCm. months: when the species is in the Baltic (1-12; migrants leave). winterMonths/winterPalette: species whose plumage changes (gulls lose the hood / get streaked heads, starlings get white spangles and a dark bill); their meshes ship a second material set M_<Id>_*_Winter. dimorphism: plumage when the female looks different (her materials M*_Female, M*_FemaleWinter), none when only size differs or not at all. femaleScale: her length relative to the male's (raptor females are larger). femaleStreamer: the outer tail feathers' length relative to his (swallow).",
